Subproblem 1: Group the software metrics into logical categories based on their role in code quality assessment, such as complexity metrics, code density metrics, Halstead metrics, McCabe metrics, and effort metrics.
Answer 1: Here is the grouping of software metrics into logical categories based on their role in code quality assessment:

1. Complexity Metrics (McCabe):  
   - complexity_balance
   - v(g) (Cyclomatic complexity)  
   - ev(g) (Essential complexity)  
   - iv(g) (Design complexity)  
   - diff_vg_ev (Cyclomatic complexity minus essential complexity)  
   - diff_complexity (Excessive cyclomatic complexity)  
   - ratio_vg_loc (Cyclomatic complexity per line of code)  
   - ratio_ivg_loc (Design complexity per line of code)  
   - ratio_vg_ivg (Balance of cyclomatic vs design complexity)

2. Code Density Metrics:  
   - loc (Line count of code)  
   - lOCode (Halstead's line count)  
   - lOBlank (Halstead's count of blank lines)  
   - locCodeAndComment (Combined code and comment)  
   - locCodeToComment (Code density per comment)

3. Halstead Metrics:  
   - uniq_Op (Unique operators)  
   - uniq_Opnd (Unique operands)  
   - n (Total operators + operands)  
   - total_Op (Total operators)  
   - total_Opnd (Total operands)  
   - v (Halstead volume)  
   - e (Halstead effort)  
   - i (Halstead intelligence)  
   - d (Halstead difficulty)  
   - b (Halstead bugs)  
   - t (Halstead time estimator)  
   - l (Halstead program length)

4. Effort Metrics:  
   - log_effort (Log-transformed effort)  
   - effort_per_operand (Effort per total operand)  
   - ratio_e_v (Effort per unit of volume)  
   - log_difficulty (Log-transformed difficulty)

5. Code/Operand Density Metrics:  
   - density_totalOpnd_loc (Operands per line of code)  
   - density_n_loc (Operations per line of code)  
   - density_totalOp_loc (Operators per line of code)  
   - ratio_n_loc (Operators and operands density normalized by code size)  

6. Categorical/Scaled Features:  
   - scaled_design_complexity (Design complexity scaled)  
   - cross_ivg_n (Design complexity scaled by operators/operands density)

This categorization provides a structured way to understand the metrics in terms of their contribution to software quality assessment.

